If there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not misapply an opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline particularly beyond an intended-use that the opioid-pain-clinical-practice-guideline has.
If there is an opioid-policy-setter then it is recommended that the opioid-policy-setter does not implement a purported-guideline-derived-policy particularly with an unintended-patient-consequence.
If there is an opioid-policy-setter then it is recommended that the opioid-policy-setter does not implement a purported-guideline-derived-policy particularly with a potentially-harmful-patient-consequence.
